## Context
Manifest validation and register payload hashing still allocate temporary vectors (`ids`, sorted shard refs) per invocation. These are lower-severity than hot claim/acquire paths but still violate strict post-startup no-allocation goals.

## Current State
Validation and hashing allocate temp vectors each call.

```rust
// crates/gossip-contracts/src/coordination/run.rs:1213-1214
let mut ids: Vec<ShardId> = shards.iter().map(|s| s.shard).collect();
ids.sort_by_key(|id| id.as_raw());
```

```rust
// crates/gossip-contracts/src/coordination/run.rs:1245-1246
let mut sorted: Vec<&InitialShardInput<'_>> = shards.iter().collect();
sorted.sort_by(|a, b| a.spec.key_range_start().cmp(b.spec.key_range_start()));
```

```rust
// crates/gossip-contracts/src/coordination/run.rs:1550-1551
let mut sorted: Vec<&InitialShardInput<'_>> = shards.iter().collect();
sorted.sort_by_key(|s| s.shard.as_raw());
```

## Desired State
Manifest validation and payload hashing run with allocation-free bounded scratch buffers or in-place strategies after startup, while preserving deterministic sort/order semantics.

## Implementation Guidance
### Files to Modify
| File | Change | Rationale |
|------|--------|-----------|
| crates/gossip-contracts/src/coordination/run.rs | Refactor validation/hash helpers to use reusable scratch / bounded inline sorting buffers | Remove transient Vec allocations |
| crates/gossip-contracts/src/coordination/in_memory.rs (if needed) | Thread scratch through register call chain | Ensure end-to-end no-allocation path |
| run tests/benchmarks | Add deterministic equivalence + allocation guard coverage | Preserve correctness and prevent regressions |

### Patterns to Follow
Leverage existing manifest size bounds (`MAX_INITIAL_SHARDS`) to define deterministic scratch capacities and avoid unbounded growth.

### Utilities to Reuse
- Existing canonical hash writer (`op_payload_hash`)
- Existing manifest constraints and validation order

### Blast Radius
- `validate_manifest`
- `hash_register_shards_payload`
- `register_shards` call path that invokes both

