## Context

`index_shard` (in_memory.rs) currently panics on allocation failure when
reserving space in the `run_shards` secondary index. This is pre-existing
behavior, not a regression from the loosen-allocation-design branch.

## Current State

`index_shard` calls `try_reserve(1).unwrap_or_else(|_| panic!(...))` in
two places (lines ~2184-2200 in in_memory.rs):
1. When reserving space in the outer `run_shards` map for a new run key
2. When reserving space in the inner `HashSet<ShardId>` for a new shard

Both paths panic on allocation failure rather than returning a Result.

## Desired State

`index_shard` should return `Result<(), RegisterShardsError>` (or a
suitable error type) so callers can handle allocation failures gracefully
and roll back partial state.

## Implementation Guidance

- Change `index_shard` signature to return `Result<bool, ...>` (or similar)
- Replace `unwrap_or_else(|_| panic!(...))` with `map_err` returning
  `ResourceExhausted { resource: "run_shards_index" }` / `"run_shards_set"`
- Update all callers of `index_shard` (split operations) to propagate errors
- Files: `crates/gossip-contracts/src/coordination/in_memory.rs`

## Code References

```rust
// in_memory.rs, index_shard method
fn index_shard(&mut self, tenant: TenantId, run: RunId, shard: ShardId) {
    let run_key = (tenant, run);
    if !self.run_shards.contains_key(&run_key) {
        self.run_shards.try_reserve(1).unwrap_or_else(|_| {
            panic!("run_shards index capacity exhausted ...")
        });
    }
    let shard_ids = self.run_shards.entry(run_key)
        .or_insert_with(|| ahash_set_with_capacity(INITIAL_CAPACITY_SMALL));
    if !shard_ids.contains(&shard) {
        shard_ids.try_reserve(1).unwrap_or_else(|_| {
            panic!("run_shards set capacity exhausted ...")
        });
    }
    shard_ids.insert(shard);
}
```

## Related Work

Related to the allocation-failure policy in CLAUDE.md (tiered allocation).
`register_shards` already handles allocation failures gracefully via
`preflight_register_capacity`; `index_shard` is the remaining gap.

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] `index_shard` returns Result instead of panicking
- [ ] All callers propagate the error
- [ ] `cargo test -p gossip-contracts` passes
- [ ] `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings` clean

